# ⚠ THIS FILE DOES NOTHING ON THE CURRENT HOST.
#
# `_redirects` is Netlify's format. This site deploys to GitHub Pages
# (.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml), which ignores the file completely — it
# is copied into dist/ as a static asset and never read by anything.
#
# That mattered: the `/* /index.html 200` line below was the SPA fallback for
# /graph, /almanac, /coverage and /about, and because it had never run, all four
# returned GitHub's own 404 page on a direct visit or a shared link. See
# docs/HANDOVER.md §9.60.
#
# The working equivalents on GitHub Pages are:
#   · a prerendered file per route  → STATIC_PAGES in scripts/prerender.mjs
#   · dist/404.html (the app shell) → written by scripts/prerender.mjs
#   · both enforced by              → scripts/check-routes-prerendered.mjs
#
# The file is kept, rather than deleted, for two reasons: it is where
# `node scripts/backfill-slugs.mjs --redirects-only` emits its legacy-slug
# block, and it is the record of a fallback that looked correct for months. If
# legacy slug redirects are ever needed, they have to be implemented client-side
# (as /shrine.html already is, via LegacyRedirect in src/App.tsx) or as real
# files — not here.

